WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.267
We bring down the bank... this is like

00:00:02.427 --> 00:00:04.227
bringing down the your mountaineering

00:00:04.227 --> 00:00:07.586
partner on the big face.

00:00:07.586 --> 00:00:08.996
You know you're tied to them. You don't

00:00:08.996 --> 00:00:10.737
really want to bring them down, because

00:00:10.737 --> 00:00:11.997
it's like--oh my god, I'm tied to them--

00:00:11.997 --> 00:00:13.526
and we're both going down. This is what was

00:00:13.526 --> 00:00:15.776
happening 02008. So there needs to

00:00:15.776 --> 00:00:17.547
be another part of the plan in place. Which

00:00:17.547 --> 00:00:19.526
simply is a government that understands

00:00:19.526 --> 00:00:22.106
that at that point the basket for saving

00:00:22.106 --> 00:00:24.057
the finance climber that you have

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:26.067
suddenly clipped their belay and they're

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:28.827
falling--the basket is this:

00:00:28.827 --> 00:00:31.767
you nationalize them. We nationalized GM in

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:34.317
02008. It worked. They paid us back.

00:00:34.317 --> 00:00:36.267
We saved their ass. The real economy needed

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:38.876
saving. Finance we paid off. We bailed out

00:00:38.876 --> 00:00:41.696
at 100 cents on the dollar to the tune

00:00:41.696 --> 00:00:45.387
of somewhere between $7 trillion and

00:00:45.387 --> 00:00:47.216
$13 trillion. I've heard both figures

00:00:47.216 --> 00:00:49.767
Friday at UCI I heard $13 trillion by

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:51.387
a very distinguished economic historian.

00:00:51.387 --> 00:00:53.337
This is because of quantitative easing,

00:00:53.337 --> 00:00:56.667
as well as the original bailout. So

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:59.877
that amount of money is kind of amazing.

00:00:59.877 --> 00:01:02.096
But this time if we've crashed the bank

00:01:02.096 --> 00:01:03.596
or if they happen to blow a bubble

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:06.386
on their own... either way we have to

00:01:06.386 --> 00:01:08.187
at that point say "Yes we'll bail you out. But

00:01:08.187 --> 00:01:11.427
now we own you ." And so now we own you

00:01:11.427 --> 00:01:14.096
means the government is the Board of Directors.

00:01:14.096 --> 00:01:16.136
That we begin to set regulations. We begin

00:01:16.136 --> 00:01:18.386
to determine loans. It would be like

00:01:18.386 --> 00:01:20.577
the federal credit union. All of these things

00:01:20.577 --> 00:01:24.057
have their precedence in earlier Public

00:01:24.057 --> 00:01:27.236
Utility District type moves. So

00:01:27.236 --> 00:01:28.977
at that point with the government taking over

00:01:28.977 --> 00:01:30.687
it would run the loan strategies,

00:01:30.687 --> 00:01:32.367
the repayment rates... and to

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:34.407
the extent that it profited the profits

00:01:34.407 --> 00:01:36.327
would just go into the Treasury. You

00:01:36.327 --> 00:01:38.607
combine that with the obvious carbon tax

00:01:38.607 --> 00:01:40.077
that we need to put on... which is

00:01:40.077 --> 00:01:42.447
not a tax but paying the true cost we need to

00:01:42.447 --> 00:01:46.447
re-conceptualize. And then also the Thomas Piketty tax

00:01:46.747 --> 00:01:50.067
which would be what he suggested 2 years ago,

00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:52.327
which is you don't just have a progressive tax

00:01:52.327 --> 00:01:55.587
on income--because people who are

00:01:55.587 --> 00:01:57.177
wealthy enough can hide their income

00:01:57.177 --> 00:01:59.007
in another country or under the rug or in

00:01:59.007 --> 00:02:01.647
future... investments in the future.

00:02:01.647 --> 00:02:03.507
So income you can hide.

00:02:03.507 --> 00:02:05.647
Capital assets--a progressive tax,

00:02:05.647 --> 00:02:07.247
sharply progressive tax

00:02:07.257 --> 00:02:09.177
on capital assets is such a game changer,

00:02:09.177 --> 00:02:12.297
such a paradigm buster, that when

00:02:12.297 --> 00:02:13.797
The Wall Street Journal and The Economist

00:02:13.797 --> 00:02:15.867
reviewed Piketty's book and they got to

00:02:15.867 --> 00:02:19.017
this last chapter... they said "Oh, but

00:02:19.017 --> 00:02:21.357
that would never work because..." and then

00:02:21.357 --> 00:02:23.457
their 500 word article ran out. And

00:02:23.457 --> 00:02:24.987
they got to stop at that point. They

00:02:24.987 --> 00:02:27.207
never said why. Because there is no why.

00:02:27.207 --> 00:02:29.607
Because it would work. And it would be an

00:02:29.607 --> 00:02:31.557
incredibly powerful tool in terms of the

00:02:31.557 --> 00:02:34.767
horizontalization of human wealth to

00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:36.747
more of the population. There's hardly a

00:02:36.747 --> 00:02:39.417
better suggestion. And Piketty's book may

00:02:39.417 --> 00:02:41.067
have been, as some people said, you know...

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:43.527
11 chapters of Marxism followed by one

00:02:43.527 --> 00:02:45.777
chapter of Keynesian reform suggestions.

00:02:45.777 --> 00:02:48.867
But, you know, I'm a Keynesian myself.

00:02:48.867 --> 00:02:50.937
I think we're in a Keynesian world. And I

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:53.307
think many people who do the 11 chapters

00:02:53.307 --> 00:02:55.497
of Marxian analysis would then like to

00:02:55.497 --> 00:02:57.117
contribute something useful that could

00:02:57.117 --> 00:02:59.817
be done right now in the world. And a tax

00:02:59.817 --> 00:03:01.107
structure is not the most

00:03:01.107 --> 00:03:03.707
radical suggestion. It's already been done before.

00:03:03.867 --> 00:03:06.847
So that would create a government surplus.

00:03:06.987 --> 00:03:08.807
Instead of government being

00:03:08.817 --> 00:03:11.877
in debt to finance forever in eternity,

00:03:11.877 --> 00:03:13.467
and therefore under the thumb of finance,

00:03:13.467 --> 00:03:15.657
government would (having a surplus)...

00:03:15.657 --> 00:03:17.427
would be in control of finance and it

00:03:17.427 --> 00:03:18.867
would have flipped the scissors-rock-

00:03:18.867 --> 00:03:21.147
paper as to who controls who. At that

00:03:21.147 --> 00:03:23.577
point, paper would...people would

00:03:23.577 --> 00:03:26.037
control governments; governmental would control

00:03:26.037 --> 00:03:27.897
finance; finance would work for the

00:03:27.897 --> 00:03:30.147
people... you would have... the the way

00:03:30.147 --> 00:03:32.007
the system needed to work. Now what would

00:03:32.007 --> 00:03:34.707
we do with that money? Health care, of course.

00:03:34.707 --> 00:03:37.647
Free public education, of course.

00:03:37.647 --> 00:03:40.077
Through college? Why not? And then also

00:03:40.077 --> 00:03:42.117
Full employment. Because full employment

00:03:42.117 --> 00:03:44.037
is another gigantic paradigm buster for

00:03:44.037 --> 00:03:46.257
Capitalism. We have 5.4%

00:03:46.257 --> 00:03:48.807
5.4% minimum unemployment. If it goes

00:03:48.807 --> 00:03:51.987
below that the market's depressed. And

00:03:51.987 --> 00:03:55.197
you want Labor wage pressure. Wage pressure

00:03:55.197 --> 00:03:57.867
is pressure on human beings lives and

00:03:57.867 --> 00:04:00.567
minds in order to keep them willing to

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:02.637
work for depressed wages--so that profits

00:04:02.637 --> 00:04:04.107
will be better. Once again it's going

00:04:04.107 --> 00:04:06.327
back to that one algorithm. So what

00:04:06.327 --> 00:04:07.707
you would want at that point with

00:04:07.707 --> 00:04:08.877
full employment, if you could always get

00:04:08.877 --> 00:04:11.217
a good living wage job from the government,

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:14.007
then private industries that existed...

00:04:14.007 --> 00:04:16.167
which would be on the margin I would

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:18.177
call it... would have to compete by giving

00:04:18.177 --> 00:04:19.826
a living wage themselves. And everybody

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:20.637
would have one

00:04:20.637 --> 00:04:23.067
along with Social Security. So what would

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:24.907
everybody do?

00:04:25.007 --> 00:04:27.987
This idea that automation is going to get rid of

00:04:27.987 --> 00:04:30.187
jobs is a very silly, bad science fiction story.

00:04:30.187 --> 00:04:31.317
It's not right. It's not going to

00:04:31.317 --> 00:04:33.477
be that way. Many things take the human

00:04:33.477 --> 00:04:35.667
touch. Taking care of young people. Taking

00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:37.677
care of old people. Taking care of sick

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:40.377
people. And also "landscape restoration".

00:04:40.377 --> 00:04:45.207
That's the environmental work of this

00:04:45.207 --> 00:04:47.847
project. Of government that's in

00:04:47.847 --> 00:04:51.837
control of the human / biosphere future,

00:04:51.837 --> 00:04:54.327
because the two are tied together. It

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:56.097
would be an enormous amount of infrastructure

00:04:56.097 --> 00:04:58.917
changes and landscape restoration in

00:04:58.917 --> 00:05:01.227
general to get us a planet where we're

00:05:01.227 --> 00:05:03.597
not using up, you know, the biosphere's

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:06.300
regenerative possibilities by August of every year.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:07.880
Which is what we're doing now.

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:10.880
But are in balance with the biosphere properly.

